f/convention-reader: spec walk (Decisions 014-042) then implementation of board items 1-2. Three defects found by fixtures rather than review — an auto-dispatched headless agent on install, a notice printed into a command substitution, and copy-mode output mistaken for a user's file. All three were invisible to reading the code and only appeared under test. Live-orchids verification (76 artifacts where the old reader laid zero) was the check that mattered; the fixture suite alone would not have proved the breakage was real.
